{
  "summary": "Validates the bucket array deserialized from `fee_estimates.dat` (or `block_policy_estimates.dat`) upon loading. Specifically, it rejects fee estimate data if the first bucket is not positive, if bucket values do not strictly increase, or if the final bucket is not infinite.",
  "problem": "When loading fee estimation history from disk, malformed or corrupted bucket lists lacking an infinite terminating bucket can cause subsequent feerate lookups to read past the end of the bucket map.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author description: 'A block_policy_estimates.dat whose bucket list lacks the infinite last bucket makes a later feerate lookup read past the end of the bucket map.'",
    "Author commit message: 'The estimator relies on the last bucket being infinite, so that every feerate finds a bucket. I reject a list whose first bucket is not positive, that does not strictly increase, or that does not end with the infinite bucket.'"
  ],
